# Copy to ".env" in the solution root (same folder as Ecommerce.API.sln) or next to the running app's working directory.
# ASP.NET Core nested config uses double underscore:
Stripe__SecretKey=sk_test_your_secret_key
Stripe__PublishableKey=pk_test_your_publishable_key
Stripe__WebhookSecret=whsec_your_signing_secret

# Optional aliases (EnvLoader copies these if Stripe__* above are empty):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# Local webhook (pick the URL that matches where the API runs):
#   dotnet / IIS:   stripe listen --forward-to https://localhost:7041/api/webhooks/stripe
#   Docker (compose): stripe listen --forward-to http://localhost:5169/api/webhooks/stripe
# Use the whsec_... printed by Stripe CLI as WebhookSecret while developing.
#
# docker-compose passes Stripe__* / STRIPE_* from this file into the api container — set at least SecretKey (and WebhookSecret for DB updates on payment success).
